				<div id="bodyContent" class="vector-body" aria-labelledby="firstHeading" data-mw-ve-target-container>
					<div class="vector-body-before-content">
							<div class="mw-indicators">
		</div>

						<div id="siteSub" class="noprint">From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia</div>
						<div id="contentSub"><div id="mw-content-subtitle"><span class="mw-redirectedfrom">(Redirected from <a href="/w/index.php?title=Stroke_(CJK_character)&amp;redirect=no" class="mw-redirect" title="Stroke (CJK character)">Stroke (CJK character)</a>)</span></div></div>
						
					</div>
					
					<div id="mw-content-text" class="mw-body-content"><div class="mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output" lang="en" dir="ltr" data-mw-parsoid-version="0.24.0.0-alpha27" data-mw-html-version="2.8.0"><section data-mw-section-id="0" id="mwAQ"><div class="shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux" style="display:none" about="#mwt1" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Short description","href":"./Template:Short_description"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Smallest writing units of Chinese characters"}},"i":0}}]}'>Smallest writing units of Chinese characters</div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_short_description"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Short_description_is_different_from_Wikidata"/></span>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"redirect","href":"./Template:Redirect"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"CJK Strokes"},"2":{"wt":"the Unicode block"},"3":{"wt":"CJK Strokes (Unicode block)"}},"i":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1368532237" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt3" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}}</style></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt2" id="mwBA">"CJK Strokes" redirects here. For the Unicode block, see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CJK_Strokes_(Unicode_block)" title="CJK Strokes (Unicode block)">CJK Strokes (Unicode block)</a>.</div>
<p class="mw-empty-elt" id="mwBQ"><span typeof="mw:Nowiki mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt4" id="mwBg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Use Oxford spelling","href":"./Template:Use_Oxford_spelling"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"March 2024"}},"i":0}}]}'></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Use_Oxford_spelling_from_March_2024" about="#mwt4"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_Wikipedia_articles_written_in_British_English_with_Oxford_spelling" about="#mwt4" id="mwBw"/></p>
<figure typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:永.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCQ"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:永.png" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/%E6%B0%B8.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled" decoding="async" loading="lazy" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="bitmap" height="300" width="300" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCg"/></a><figcaption id="mwCw"><span lang="zh" about="#mwt5" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"wikt-lang","href":"./Template:Wikt-lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh"},"2":{"wt":"永"}},"i":0}}]}'><a rel="mw:WikiLink/Interwiki" href="https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/永#Chinese" title="wikt:永" class="extiw">永</a></span> 'forever' or 'permanence', a Chinese character that represents a variety of strokes, and is often used to demonstrate the major stroke categories</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwDQ">Strokes (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simplified_Chinese_characters" title="Simplified Chinese characters" about="#mwt6" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"lang-zh","href":"./Template:Lang-zh"},"params":{"t":{"wt":"筆畫"},"s":{"wt":"笔画"},"p":{"wt":"bǐhuà"}},"i":0}}]}'>simplified Chinese</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt6">:</span><span about="#mwt6"> </span><span lang="zh-Hans" about="#mwt6"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_simplified_Chinese-language_text"/>笔画</span><span about="#mwt6">; </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Traditional_Chinese_characters" title="Traditional Chinese characters" about="#mwt6">traditional Chinese</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt6">:</span><span about="#mwt6"> </span><span lang="zh-Hant" about="#mwt6"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_traditional_Chinese-language_text"/>筆畫</span><span about="#mwt6">; </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinyin" title="Pinyin" about="#mwt6">pinyin</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt6">:</span><span about="#mwt6"> </span><i about="#mwt6" id="mwDw"><span lang="zh-Latn">bǐhuà</span></i>) are the smallest structural units making up written <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_characters" title="Chinese characters" id="mwEA">Chinese characters</a>. In the act of writing, a stroke is defined as a movement of a writing instrument on a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Writing_material" title="Writing material" id="mwEQ">writing material</a> surface, or 
the trace left on the surface from a discrete application of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Writing_implement" title="Writing implement" id="mwEg">writing implement</a>.<sup about="#mwt7" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESu201474_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESu201474"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESu201474-1"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Su"},"2":{"wt":"2014"},"p":{"wt":"74"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESu201474-1" id="mwEw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFQ">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFg">]</span></span></a></sup> The modern sense of discretized strokes first came into being with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clerical_script" title="Clerical script" id="mwFw">clerical script</a> during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Han_dynasty" title="Han dynasty" id="mwGA">Han dynasty</a>.<sup about="#mwt10" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESu201474–75_2-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESu201474–75"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESu201474–75-2"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Su"},"2":{"wt":"2014"},"pp":{"wt":"74–75"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESu201474–75-2" id="mwGQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGw">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHA">]</span></span></a></sup> In the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regular_script" title="Regular script" id="mwHQ">regular script</a> that emerged during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tang_dynasty" title="Tang dynasty" id="mwHg">Tang dynasty</a>—the most recent major style, highly studied for its aesthetics in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Asian_calligraphy" title="East Asian calligraphy" class="mw-redirect" id="mwHw">East Asian calligraphy</a>—individual strokes are discrete and highly regularized. By contrast, the ancient <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seal_script" title="Seal script" id="mwIA">seal script</a> has line terminals within characters that are often unclear, making them non-trivial to count.</p>

<p id="mwIQ">Study and classification of strokes is useful for understanding <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_calligraphy" title="Chinese calligraphy" id="mwIg">Chinese character calligraphy</a>, ensuring character legibility, identifying fundamental components of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radical_(Chinese_characters)" title="Radical (Chinese characters)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwIw">radicals</a>, and implementing support for the writing system on computers.</p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwJA" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwJQ" aria-labelledby="Evolution"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Evolution">Evolution</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Chinese_character_strokes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: Evolution"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwJg">The terminals of the individual marks in ancient character forms are often unclear, and it is sometimes nontrivial to count them. The modern motion of discretized strokes did not fully emerge until <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clerical_script" title="Clerical script" id="mwJw">clerical script</a>:<sup about="#mwt13" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESu201474–75Qiu201374–79_3-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESu201474–75Qiu201374–79"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESu201474–75Qiu201374–79-3"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnm","href":"./Template:Sfnm"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Su"},"2":{"wt":"2014"},"1pp":{"wt":"74-75"},"3":{"wt":"Qiu"},"4":{"wt":"2013"},"2pp":{"wt":"74-79"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESu201474–75Qiu201374–79-3" id="mwKA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKg">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<table class="wikitable" style="text-align: center" about="#mwt16" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwLA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Chinese script ma3 evo","href":"./Template:Chinese_script_ma3_evo"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'>
<caption>Historical evolution of the character <span style="font-weight:normal; font-style:normal"><span lang="zh-Hant"><span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_traditional_Chinese-language_text"/></span>馬</span> 'horse'</span></caption>
<tbody><tr>
<th rowspan="2" scope="col">Oracle</th><th rowspan="2" scope="col">Bronze</th><th colspan="2" scope="col">Seal</th><th rowspan="2">Clerical</th><th colspan="2" scope="col">Regular</th></tr>
<tr>
<th scope="col">Large</th><th scope="col">Small</th><th scope="col">Traditional</th><th scope="col">Simplified</th></tr>
<tr>
<td scope="row"><span class="skin-invert" typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:馬-oracle.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:馬-oracle.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/%E9%A6%AC-oracle.svg/60px-%E9%A6%AC-oracle.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/%E9%A6%AC-oracle.svg/120px-%E9%A6%AC-oracle.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="60" width="60" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></td><td><span class="skin-invert" typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:馬-bronze.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:馬-bronze.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/%E9%A6%AC-bronze.svg/60px-%E9%A6%AC-bronze.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/%E9%A6%AC-bronze.svg/120px-%E9%A6%AC-bronze.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="60" width="60" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></td><td><span class="skin-invert" typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:馬-bigseal.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:馬-bigseal.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/%E9%A6%AC-bigseal.svg/60px-%E9%A6%AC-bigseal.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/%E9%A6%AC-bigseal.svg/120px-%E9%A6%AC-bigseal.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="60" width="60" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></td><td><span class="skin-invert" typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:馬-seal.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:馬-seal.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/%E9%A6%AC-seal.svg/60px-%E9%A6%AC-seal.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/%E9%A6%AC-seal.svg/120px-%E9%A6%AC-seal.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="60" width="60" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></td><td><span class="skin-invert" typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:馬-clerical.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:馬-clerical.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/%E9%A6%AC-clerical-han.svg/60px-%E9%A6%AC-clerical-han.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/%E9%A6%AC-clerical-han.svg/120px-%E9%A6%AC-clerical-han.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="60" width="60" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></td><td><span class="skin-invert" typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:馬-kaishu.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:馬-kaishu.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/%E9%A6%AC-kaishu.svg/60px-%E9%A6%AC-kaishu.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/%E9%A6%AC-kaishu.svg/120px-%E9%A6%AC-kaishu.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="60" width="60" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></td><td><span class="skin-invert" typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:马-kaishu.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:马-kaishu.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/%E9%A9%AC-kaishu.svg/60px-%E9%A9%AC-kaishu.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/%E9%A9%AC-kaishu.svg/120px-%E9%A9%AC-kaishu.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="60" width="60" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></td></tr>
</tbody></table>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwLQ" aria-labelledby="Purpose"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Purpose">Purpose</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Chinese_character_strokes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Purpose"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwLg">The study and classification of strokes is used for:</p>
<ol id="mwLw"><li id="mwMA">understanding <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_calligraphy" title="Chinese calligraphy" id="mwMQ">Chinese character calligraphy</a> – the correct method of writing, shape formation and stroke order required for character legibility;</li>
<li id="mwMg">understanding stroke changes according to the style that is in use;</li>
<li id="mwMw"><figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwNA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Upper_Lascar_Row,_Hong_Kong_(2051987459).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwNQ"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Upper_Lascar_Row,_Hong_Kong_(2051987459).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Upper_Lascar_Row%2C_Hong_Kong_%282051987459%29.jpg/250px-Upper_Lascar_Row%2C_Hong_Kong_%282051987459%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Upper_Lascar_Row%2C_Hong_Kong_%282051987459%29.jpg/500px-Upper_Lascar_Row%2C_Hong_Kong_%282051987459%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2221" data-file-height="3071" data-file-type="bitmap" height="346" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwNg"/></a><figcaption id="mwNw">Traditional <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ink_brush" title="Ink brush" id="mwOA">calligraphy brushes</a> which give the strokes their unique shape</figcaption></figure>defining stroke naming and counting conventions;</li>
<li id="mwOQ">identifying fundamental components of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radical_(Chinese_characters)" title="Radical (Chinese characters)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwOg">Han radicals</a>; and</li>
<li id="mwOw">their use in computing.</li></ol>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwPA" aria-labelledby="Formation"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Formation">Formation</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Chinese_character_strokes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: Formation"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwPQ">When writing Han radicals, a single stroke includes all the motions necessary to produce a given part of a character before lifting the writing instrument from the writing surface; thus, a single stroke may have abrupt changes in direction within the line. For example:</p>
<ul id="mwPg"><li id="mwPw"><span class="skin-invert" typeof="mw:File" id="mwQA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cjk_k_str_v.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwQQ"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cjk_k_str_v.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Cjk_k_str_v.svg/40px-Cjk_k_str_v.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Cjk_k_str_v.svg/60px-Cjk_k_str_v.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="512" data-file-height="512" data-file-type="drawing" height="30" width="30" class="mw-file-element" id="mwQg"/></a></span> (Vertical / <i id="mwQw"><span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt17" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwRA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh-Latn-pinyin"},"2":{"wt":"shù"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="zh-Latn-pinyin">shù</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt17" id="mwRQ"/></i>) is classified as a basic stroke because it is a single stroke that forms a line moving in one direction.</li>
<li id="mwRg"><span class="skin-invert" typeof="mw:File" id="mwRw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cjk_k_str_vhv.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwSA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cjk_k_str_vhv.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Cjk_k_str_vhv.svg/40px-Cjk_k_str_vhv.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Cjk_k_str_vhv.svg/60px-Cjk_k_str_vhv.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="512" data-file-height="512" data-file-type="drawing" height="30" width="30" class="mw-file-element" id="mwSQ"/></a></span> (Vertical – Horizontal – Vertical / <span title="Chinese-language text" about="#mwt18" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwSg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"zh-Latn-pinyin"},"2":{"wt":"shù zhé zhé"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="zh-Latn-pinyin">shù zhé zhé</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Chinese-language_text" about="#mwt18" id="mwSw"/>) is classified as a compound stroke because it is a single stroke that forms a line that includes one or more abrupt changes in direction. This example is a sequence of three basic strokes written without lifting the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Writing_instrument" title="Writing instrument" class="mw-redirect" id="mwTA">writing instrument</a> such as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ink_brush" title="Ink brush" id="mwTQ">ink brush</a> from the writing surface.</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwTg" aria-labelledby="Direction"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Direction">Direction</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Chinese_character_strokes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: Direction"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwTw">All strokes have direction.  They are unidirectional and start from one entry point. As such, they are usually not written in the reverse direction by native users.  Here are some examples:</p>
<ul class="gallery mw-gallery-traditional skin-invert" typeof="mw:Extension/gallery" about="#mwt19" id="mwUA" data-mw='{"name":"gallery","attrs":{"class":"skin-invert","widths":"100px","heights":"100px"},"body":{}}'>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 135px;" id="mwUQ"><div class="thumb" style="width: 130px; height: 130px;" id="mwUg"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwUw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:丶-order.gif" class="mw-file-description" id="mwVA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:丶-order.gif" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/%E4%B8%B6-order.gif/120px-%E4%B8%B6-order.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/%E4%B8%B6-order.gif/250px-%E4%B8%B6-order.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="bitmap" height="100" width="100" class="mw-file-element" id="mwVQ"/></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwVg"></div></li>
